# Opalescence makes Humility a creature, so Turn to Frog can target it. On turn 4 Bot2 casts it at Humility: in layer 6
# Turn to Frog's "loses all abilities" would take Humility's ability away, so Humility's effect depends on it and waits
# (CR 613.8a); applied first, it leaves Humility with no ability to apply at all - and as that ability's effect begins in
# layer 6, no part of it has begun to apply earlier to go on applying (CR 613.6). Until end of turn Humility does nothing:
# Bot1's Inspiring Overseer is its printed 2/1 with flying again. Humility is a blue Frog enchantment creature, 1/1 (layer
# 7b: Opalescence's 4/4 first, the later Turn to Frog's 1/1 after). On turn 5, the frog gone in the cleanup (CR 514.2),
# Humility applies again: the Overseer is 1/1 without flying and Humility a 1/1 enchantment creature with no Frog type.
# (Under Humility from turn 3 the Overseer was 1/1 without flying; its enters trigger on turn 1 drew Humility.)

